  {
    "name": "task_plan",
    "description": "Plan code, repository research and other multi-step work for coding Agents, one supervised task per independent piece. Check machines_list and agents_list first; follow-up for an Agent with the context goes to agent_send. Read-only, user_requested and preapproved tasks start at once, others on the owner's Start; a queued receipt is not a started Agent.\n\nWrite title (under 20 characters), why, goal, done_when and out_of_bounds in Simplified Chinese. A writable task needs checkable done_when, a read-only one goal. Continue a task with continues (scope_revision after task_scope); retry a failed start with task_retry. readonly=true: Claude-family launchers run with bypassPermissions; Codex and agy (Antigravity companion) in plan mode, or with assistant.readonly_mode=prompt by instruction only, not a security boundary; pi and cursor refuse it.\n\n`wait_seconds` observes up to 50 seconds after dispatch, appending `Inline observation` JSON: `completed`(this input's `reply`), `question`(pending `interaction_id`), `timeout`/`cancelled`/`unavailable`/`interrupted`/`failed`, with known input/session ids. Observation never answers questions, accepts tasks, resends or cancels work; normal supervision/`task_review` applies. Older nodes may time out rather than return an unrelated reply. Only an immediately dispatchable single-task plan waits.\n\nDetails: read .claude/skills/persona-work/references/task-plan.md in your working directory.",
    "input_schema": {
